re used to implement \npriority queues efficiently, especially in algorithms that perform many decrease-key \nand insert operations. It consists of a collection of trees that follow the min-heap \nproperty, where the smallest key is always stored at a node pointed to by a minimum \npointer. Unlike binomial heaps, Fibonacci heaps perform insert and merge \noperations lazily, postponing restructuring until an extract-min operation is \nexecuted. This lazy strategy allows Fibonacci heaps to achieve excellent amortized \ntime complexities, with constant-time insertion and decrease-key operations and \nlogarithmic-time extract-min, making them particularly useful in graph algorithms \nsuch as Dijkstra’s and Prim’s algorithms. \nAlgorithm : \n", "embedding": {"5(b)": 0.008620689655172414, "aim:": 0.008620689655172414, "to": 0.034482758620689655, "implement": 0.017241379310344827, "fibonacci": 0.034482758620689655, "heap": 0.017241379310344827, "description": 0.008620689655172414, ":": 0.017241379310344827, "a": 0.034482758620689655, "is": 0.02586206896551724, "an": 0.017241379310344827, "advanced": 0.008620689655172414, "heap-based": 0.008620689655172414, "data": 0.008620689655172414, "structure": 0.008620689655172414, "used": 0.008620689655172414, "priority": 0.008620689655172414, "queues": 0.008620689655172414, "efficiently,": 0.008620689655172414, "especially": 0.008620689655172414, "in": 0.017241379310344827, "algorithms": 0.017241379310344827, "that": 0.017241379310344827, "perform": 0.017241379310344827, "many": 0.008620689655172414, "decrease-key": 0.017241379310344827, "and": 0.04310344827586207, "insert": 0.017241379310344827, "operations.": 0.008620689655172414, "it": 0.008620689655172414, "consists": 0.008620689655172414, "of": 0.017241379310344827, "collection": 0.008620689655172414, "trees": 0.008620689655172414, "follow": 0.008620689655172414, "the": 0.017241379310344827, "min-heap": 0.008620689655172414, "property,": 0.008620689655172414, "where": 0.008620689655172414, "smallest": 0.008620689655172414, "key": 0.008620689655172414, "always": 0.008620689655172414, "stored": 0.008620689655172414, "at": 0.008620689655172414, "node": 0.008620689655172414, "pointed": 0.008620689655172414, "by": 0.008620689655172414, "minimum": 0.008620689655172414, "pointer.": 0.008620689655172414, "unlike": 0.008620689655172414, "binomial": 0.008620689655172414, "heaps,": 0.008620689655172414, "heaps": 0.017241379310344827, "merge": 0.008620689655172414, "operations": 0.017241379310344827, "lazily,": 0.008620689655172414, "postponing": 0.008620689655172414, "restructuring": 0.008620689655172414, "until": 0.008620689655172414, "extract-min": 0.008620689655172414, "operation": 0.008620689655172414, "executed.": 0.008620689655172414, "this": 0.008620689655172414, "lazy": 0.008620689655172414, "strategy": 0.008620689655172414, "allows": 0.008620689655172414, "achieve": 0.008620689655172414, "excellent": 0.008620689655172414, "amortized": 0.008620689655172414, "time": 0.008620689655172414, "complexities,": 0.008620689655172414, "with": 0.008620689655172414, "constant-time": 0.008620689655172414, "insertion": 0.008620689655172414, "logarithmic-time": 0.008620689655172414, "extract-min,": 0.008620689655172414, "making": 0.008620689655172414, "them": 0.008620689655172414, "particularly": 0.008620689655172414, "useful": 0.008620689655172414, "graph": 0.008620689655172414, "such": 0.008620689655172414, "as": 0.008620689655172414, "dijkstra’s": 0.008620689655172414, "prim’s": 0.008620689655172414, "algorithms.": 0.008620689655172414, "algorithm": 0.008620689655172414}, "source_file": "my_document.pdf", "page_number": 3}, {"id": "5cc3105a-7beb-4e7a-9565-6fb9c97d0250", "text": "Algorithm: INSERT(x) in Fibonacci Heap \nInput: An element x \nOutput: Updated Fibonacci heap after insertion \n1. Create a new node with key x. \n2. Initialize the node’s degree as 0, and set its parent and child pointers to \nNULL. \n3. Add the new node to the root list of the heap. \n4. If the heap is empty or x is smaller than the current minimum key, update the \nminimum pointer to this node. \n5. Increment the total number of nodes in the heap. \n6. Return the updated heap. \n \n \n \n \nAlgorithm: EXTRACT-MIN() in Fibonacci Heap \nInput: A Fibonacci heap H \nOutput: Minimum key element or EMPTY \n1. If the heap is empty, return EMPTY. \n2. Let z be the node pointed to by the minimum pointer. \n3. For each child of z: \no Remove the child from z’s child list. \no Add the child to the root list of the heap. \no Set the child’s parent to NULL. \n4. Remove node z from the root list. \n5. If z was the only node, set the minimum pointer to NULL. \n", "embedding": {"algorithm:": 0.011299435028248588, "insert(x)": 0.005649717514124294, "in": 0.01694915254237288, "fibonacci": 0.022598870056497175, "heap": 0.03389830508474576, "input:": 0.011299435028248588, "an": 0.005649717514124294, "element": 0.011299435028248588, "x": 0.011299435028248588, "output:": 0.011299435028248588, "updated": 0.011299435028248588, "after": 0.005649717514124294, "insertion": 0.005649717514124294, "1.": 0.011299435028248588, "create": 0.005649717514124294, "a": 0.011299435028248588, "new": 0.011299435028248588, "node": 0.022598870056497175, "with": 0.005649717514124294, "key": 0.011299435028248588, "x.": 0.005649717514124294, "2.": 0.011299435028248588, "initialize": 0.005649717514124294, "the": 0.11864406779661017, "node’s": 0.005649717514124294, "degree": 0.005649717514124294, "as": 0.005649717514124294, "0,": 0.005649717514124294, "and": 0.011299435028248588, "set": 0.01694915254237288, "its": 0.005649717514124294, "parent": 0.011299435028248588, "child": 0.02824858757062147, "pointers": 0.005649717514124294, "to": 0.03954802259887006, "null.": 0.01694915254237288, "3.": 0.011299435028248588, "add": 0.011299435028248588, "root": 0.01694915254237288, "list": 0.011299435028248588, "of": 0.022598870056497175, "heap.": 0.022598870056497175, "4.": 0.011299435028248588